					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-10-12 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br>Warm                        militant greetings with a smile. Geo here with an update.                        <br />                       <br />                       More and more folks are hitting us up on some &quot;When&#39;s                        Gabe&#39;s <em>Lovework</em> album going to drop?&quot; Easy,                        star. The album artwork is done - a masterpiece from Overstand                        artist <strong>Darvin Vida</strong> and designer <strong><a href="http://www.wilmergalindo.com/" target="new">Wilmer                        Galindo</a></strong> (who designed the Blue Scholars <em>The                        Long March EP </em>and Common Market self-titled album art).                        The production on the record is incredible, with 206 vet                        <strong>Amos Miller</strong> handling the bulk of the production,                        with additional cuts produced by <strong>Kitone</strong>,                        <strong>Moka Only</strong> and ya boy <strong>Sabzi</strong>!<br />                       <br />                       But instead of sitting and waiting for <em>Lovework,</em>                        get your GT fix with his previous musical body of work.                        If you haven&#39;t yet, go get a copy of <strong><a href="http://www.abcreole.com/">Abyssinian                        Creole&#39;s</a></strong> 2005 album <em>Sexy Beast</em>, featuring                        Gabriel Teodros with counterpart <strong>Khingz Makoma</strong>                        (aka Khalil Crisis). Gabriel is also posting up exclusive                        and unreleased tracks on his <a href="http://profile.myspace.com/index.cfm?fuseaction=user.viewprofile&amp;friendid=18445">myspace                        page</a> every week. Free downloads for the people!<br />                       <br />                       Also, pick up this week&#39;s copy of <em>The Stranger</em>                        and check out page 13 for an <a href="http://www.thestranger.com/seattle/Content?oid=87909" target="new">article                        on the current <strong>FBI harassment and monitoring of                        the Seattle Filipino activist community</strong></a><strong>                        that I work with,</strong> including the homie/teacher/organizer                        Freedom Allah Siyam and my family. The support has been                        beautiful, the struggle continues, the music won&#39;t stop.<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=285">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[46]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=230">[47]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=235">[48]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=240">[49]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=245">[50]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=250">[51]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=255">[52]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=260">[53]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=265">[54]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=270">[55]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=275">[56]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=280">[57]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=285">[58]</A> [59] [&gt;&gt;] </span></p>
